# ---- release notes / docs ----
write('releases/2.0.0-rc.1.md', '''# PlexonTravel 2.0.0-rc.1\n\nPhase 2 release candidate. Runtime certification is intentionally pending.\n\n## Phase 2\n- Authoritative per-player attempt identity now starts before safe destination resolution and remains owned through async teleport terminal state.\n- Duplicate warmup/in-flight requests are rejected rather than replacing active travel.\n- Fee ownership has a single compensation path and executing attempts cannot be cancelled out from under their terminal callback.\n- Warp deletion is actor/action/warp/revision-bound, expiring and one-shot.\n- `renamewarp` updates display metadata while preserving stable warp IDs.\n- Warp browser exposes locked state and default fee context.\n- Candidate configuration is validated before reload activation; malformed reloads retain the prior known-good runtime.\n- PlaceholderAPI expansion exposes cached-only travel state.\n- CI now certifies Java 25/class-major 69, provided-dependency boundaries, test totals, provenance and checksum assets.\n\n## Compatibility\nThe focused `/spawn`, `/hub`, `/back`, `/warp`, `/warps`, `/ptravel` and travel administration product remains intact. Existing SQLite destination/warp/back schema is preserved; no destructive database migration is required from v1.0.1.\n\n## Certification boundary\nGitHub source/tag CI is not PlexonCraft runtime certification. Production migration, command ownership, TheosisEconomy/Vault behavior, restart/soak, PlaceholderAPI, interoperability and Spark/MSPT gates remain pending.\n''')
